// QuicBaaS Per-Tenant Barrier Protocol Buffer Definitions v1
// Per-tenant barrier lifecycle exposed by the QuicBaaS daemon.
//
// QuicBaaS itself owns no per-tenant barrier logic; the embedded go-qrdb
// instance does. These RPCs are a thin gRPC facade so that gRPC-only clients
// connecting to the QuicBaaS endpoint can drive per-tenant barrier operations
// without dialling qrdb directly. The shape mirrors the REST surface served
// from /api/v1/tenants/{tenant_id}/barrier/* and the underlying go-qrdb
// TenantBarrierService.
//
// Authorization: callers must hold tenant_barrier:{init,unseal,seal,status}
// for the target tenant. The system tenant is denied at the transport layer
// before these RPCs are reached.
